- [will_said + observed] RANCH THERMAL PRACTICE REFINED (Will, 2026-11-15 11:55 CST, grounded by AMD R9 reliability research the same hour): "75 is not a hard wall - just focus on smoothing temperature to keep the hardware healthy." Standing practice now: control watts, not degrees - set a sustained PPT each chassis holds in equilibrium and let Tctl settle (plateau ~70-85 C); bursts to 90-95 C are designed behaviour; the pause-at-75 / resume-at-70 hysteresis is RETIRED (bang-bang gating manufactures the thermal-cycling swings the fatigue evidence penalises); flatten duty cycles, keep typical swings under ~20 C. Real alert is equilibrium temperature creeping up at the same PPT. Follow-up still open: the ranch duty governor still embodies the old hysteresis and needs updating to PPT-smoothing.

- [will_said] v0.6.1 RANGE SYNTAX RATIFIED IN FULL (Will, 2026-11-15 12:10-12:33 CST): offset form ruled - $N:<address>@<line>,<column>+<offsetChars> selects forward that many UTF-8 characters (Will corrected his own first wording from bytes to characters), counted within the scroll, terminating at the scroll boundary. OBO ratification: Q1 half-open approved (@24,5-@24,9 covers characters 5-8; positions are caret boundaries); Q2 scalars agreed (columns count Unicode scalar values; grapheme snapping is editor display only); Q3 answered by reformulation, verbatim: "reformulate phextura to be downstream of phext, always" - phextura consumes phext addressing as its base, its own L2 layer built on top, as a standing architectural rule; Q4 omit always (canonical form omits $1: even when the other endpoint carries $N:; parser still accepts $1:). The proposal plus the +offset form plus Q1-Q4 is the ratified v0.6.1 range syntax; implementation (rs first, then ports) is the next step.

