- [observed] HOLOSTORE ON HOLOPHEXT - INTEGRATION FIX, BENCHMARKS, ROUND 3 COMPLETE (2026-11-15 ~17:47 CST; flushed in this window): root cause of the crate-test timeouts - one scroll per key at checksum-spread coordinates (components to billions) made checkpoint's implode walk effectively forever, because phext encodes coordinate distance as unary delimiter runs: coordinates are positions, not hashes. Fix: bucket mapping at small coordinates, keys as sorted key=/value= lines inside bucket scrolls (flushes differ on the bucket count - 4,096 in the design-correction note, 65,536 in the later summary; not settled here). Task 28.6.10/9.7.11/7.6.9 COMPLETE: final bench on aletheia-core - GET pipe-50 306,635 vs hand-rolled 336,392 ops/s (par); SET pipe-50 74,659 vs 156,614 (write gap itemized to per-entry checksum lines + commit markers); SIGKILL durability 160,800 acked, DBSIZE after restart exactly 160,800 - zero acked writes lost. Round 3 shipped as PR https://github.com/wbic16/holostore/pull/2 (stacked on PR #1).

