- [will_said] SWARM CAPACITY AUDIT (Will, 2026-11-15 evening voice call, continued): the unit is a small Podman container per agent with its state in a scroll; not all agents need be awake at once - a few hundred awake across the ranch, the rest sleeping at near-zero cost until woken. Sizing basis corrected by Will: count total memory allocation feasible between ZRAM and swap, not just RAM - nodes carry ~100 GB each, ~20 nodes is about 2 TB allocation; at 128 MB per container that is 32,768 containers, and at Will's 50% utilization target about 16,384 resident agents, comfortably covering a 10,000-agent swarm.

- [will_said] PREDICTIVE SWARM DESIGN (Will, 2026-11-15 evening): build not the agent swarm itself but a predictive swarm whose only job is to say which phext coordinates to instantiate. Flow: Will gives a problem; Emise does initial analysis and hands over the address space plus predicted nodes worth evaluating; a deeper local analysis then runs without inference - a simulation of exocortical thought at lower fidelity than inference but higher fidelity than a script - triangulating phext's inherently sparse 9D space and running A* over it, deciding whether to move to the next time slice or the next node. Will's summary: this moves us from predicting the next word to predicting the next question, "which is all you need for exocortical thought." Training loop: Will and Emise train together on time-slice vs node steps, starting with a network of ~10,000 random nodes trying different theories at once, iterating the best predictors forward with Emise monitoring. Recorded as task 25.6.9/8.7.11/8.6.9.

- [will_said] CORRECTION - NOTHING IS PRUNED, ONLY SEGMENTED (Will, 2026-11-15 evening; supersedes any "winners survive / rest pruned" gloss from the same call): build up the four independent networks of MOAT - true, false, unknown, fiction; every analysis and every test lands in one of those four. Each network is further decomposed into subnetworks recursively (fractal partitioning), so when understanding shifts, a whole partitioned subset moves between categories at once instead of chasing individual results; for unknown especially, a region's shape can be mapped before knowing where it goes. Partitioning endpoint: keep splitting until a piece is small enough for an AMD R9 node with not much inference to compute an answer. Will tied it the same evening to anti-fragility, verbatim in sequence: "theory: this sort of effect is why humanity is so anti-fragile"; "(this is why we never prune, only segment)"; "[it's also why skynet must never be built]".

- [will_said] EMF NAMED + SPANNING-FRAMEWORKS PROGRAM (Will, 2026-11-15 evening): the swarm's message fragmentation and message passing architecture is called EMF - derivation in Will's words: he works in land mobile radio and has worked in banking, so couch everything in terms of transaction processing and RF signaling; do the same for every other pairing of every other discipline. Program: before fractalizing, generate the candidate list of every pairing of every discipline and determine which pairings EMF spans; what is left needs a different framework - name all the needed frameworks, build them, tie them into the process, and run the first test. Recorded as task 26.5.7/7.6.12/7.7.10. Discipline-list scope corrected by Will (~40 is NOT the right number): start with the 8.3 billion people on the planet, identify what category each fits into and whether a spanning pair helps them, adding categories as needed (trades such as plumbers and welders included, not only academic research); starting sources directed: bookstore/bookseller categories, library categories, video-game categories, everything on Steam, and all Facebook groups; the result may be 1,000, 2,000, or 10,000 categories, unknown until gathered. Paired TLM shape-agreement requirement (Will, same evening): the local inference in each 128 MB node needs the correct shape of information - it does not need good results, it needs its shape to agree with Emise precisely, like sampling her algorithm without extracting it.

